#!/bin/sh
# vms: the machine's shared virtual machines, in $COWORKER_HOME/vms (COWORKER_HOME is ~/coworker
# unless set), used by one project at a time. README.md, "VMs".
#
#   vms claim   VM PROJECT                                PROJECT needs VM
#   vms release VM PROJECT                                PROJECT is done with VM (never deletes it)
#   vms run     VM DIR [--keep-vm] [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...]
#                                                         the one call: claim VM with DIR's needs of
#                                                         it, merge every claimant's, lock, start it
#                                                         if it's down, check it, run COMMAND, stop it
#                                                         if this run started it
#   vms lock    VM PROJECT [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...]  run COMMAND holding VM's lock
#   vms env     VM                                        how to reach VM, as assignments to eval
#   vms list                                              every VM, its claims, and who holds it
#   vms create  VM [--yes]                                build VM from its recipe ($COWORKER_HOME/recipes/VM),
#                                                         replacing the one there (a human's call: --yes)
#   vms update  VM                                        Windows Update until nothing is left, under the lock
#
# Beside each VM's folder (its README.md and vm.env): an empty VM.<project> per project that claims
# it, and VM.lock, which names the holder while a run holds it.
set -eu
HOMEDIR=${COWORKER_HOME:-$HOME/coworker}
DIR=$HOMEDIR/vms
RECIPES=$HOMEDIR/recipes
USAGE="usage: vms run VM DIR [--keep-vm] [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...] | claim VM PROJECT | release VM PROJECT | lock VM PROJECT [--no-wait] -- COMMAND [ARG...] | env VM | list | create VM [--yes] | update VM"
DEPS="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)/deps"
usage() { echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2; }

project() {     # project NAME: exit 2 unless NAME can be a project's name
    case $1 in ''|*[!A-Za-z0-9_-]*|lock) echo "vms: a project name is letters, digits, - and _ (and isn't lock)" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
}
client() {      # the installed half of the handshake: a call that changes shared state comes through a
                # project's coworker submodule, which passes its protocol (README.md, "Protocol"); exit 3
    mine=$(cat "$(dirname "$0")/../PROTOCOL" 2>/dev/null || true)
    c=${COWORKER_CLIENT_PROTOCOL:-}
    if [ -z "$c" ]; then
        echo "vms: called directly, not through a project's coworker submodule: a project calls <its checkout>/coworker/bin/vms (coworker ${mine:-?}; README.md, \"In a project\")" >&2
        exit 3
    fi
    case $c.$mine in *[!0-9.]*|*..*) echo "vms: can't read the protocols (this project's '$c', installed '$mine')" >&2; exit 3 ;; esac
    if [ "${c%%.*}" != "${mine%%.*}" ] || [ "${mine#*.}" -lt "${c#*.}" ]; then
        echo "vms: this project's coworker is protocol $c and the installed one is $mine: the machine's owner moves them together (README.md, \"Protocol\")" >&2
        exit 3
    fi
}

claims_of() {   # claims_of VM: the projects that claim VM, each after a space
    out=""
    for f in "$DIR/$1".*; do
        [ -f "$f" ] || continue
        s=${f#"$DIR/$1".}
        case $s in *.*|lock) ;; *) out="$out $s" ;; esac
    done
    echo "$out"
}

claim() {
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); P=$2
    project "$P"
    mkdir -p "$DIR"
    touch "$DIR/$VM.$P"
    if [ -f "$DIR/$VM/vm.env" ]; then echo "$P claims $VM"; else echo "$P claims $VM, not set up yet: no $DIR/$VM/vm.env"; fi
}

release() {     # a VM is never deleted by a script: with the last claim gone this says so, and the owner decides
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); P=$2
    rm -f "$DIR/$VM.$P"
    left=$(claims_of "$VM")
    if [ -z "$left" ]; then
        echo "$P released $VM; no project claims it now: ask the machine's owner before deleting $DIR/$VM"
    else
        echo "$P released $VM; kept, claimed by$left"
    fi
}

lock() {        # COMMAND sees COWORKER_VM_LOCKED=<vm>; --no-wait exits 75 when another run holds it
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); P=$2
    shift 2
    WAIT=1
    [ "${1:-}" = --no-wait ] && { WAIT=0; shift; }
    [ "${1:-}" = -- ] || { echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2; }
    shift
    [ $# -gt 0 ] || { echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2; }
    [ -d "$DIR/$VM" ] || { echo "vms: no VM $VM in $DIR" >&2; exit 1; }
    L="$DIR/$VM.lock"
    exec 9>>"$L"
    if ! flock -n 9; then
        who=$(cat "$L" 2>/dev/null || true)
        [ "$WAIT" = 1 ] || { echo "$VM is in use: ${who:-by another run}" >&2; exit 75; }
        echo "$VM is in use: ${who:-by another run}; waiting for it"
        flock 9
    fi
    printf '%s, pid %s, since %s\n' "$P" "$$" "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z')" > "$L"
    COWORKER_VM_LOCKED=$VM
    export COWORKER_VM_LOCKED
    rc=0
    "$@" || rc=$?
    : > "$L"
    exit "$rc"
}

env_of() {      # VM_HOME and each VM_* setting in vm.env, with the key and known-hosts paths made absolute
    [ $# -ge 1 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1")
    H="$DIR/$VM"
    [ -f "$H/vm.env" ] || { echo "vms: no $H/vm.env (README.md, \"vm.env\")" >&2; exit 1; }
    H=$(cd "$H" && pwd -P)
    q() { printf "'%s'" "$(printf '%s' "$1" | sed "s/'/'\\\\''/g")"; }
    (
        unset VM_OS VM_CONTAINER VM_SSH_HOST VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY VM_KNOWN_HOSTS
        . "$H/vm.env"
        for k in VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY; do
            eval "v=\${$k:-}"
            [ -n "$v" ] || { echo "vms: $H/vm.env sets no $k" >&2; exit 1; }
        done
        abs() { case $1 in /*) printf '%s' "$1" ;; ?*) printf '%s/%s' "$H" "$1" ;; esac; }
        echo "VM_HOME=$(q "$H")"
        echo "VM_OS=$(q "${VM_OS:-}")"
        echo "VM_CONTAINER=$(q "${VM_CONTAINER:-}")"
        echo "VM_SSH_HOST=$(q "${VM_SSH_HOST:-127.0.0.1}")"
        echo "VM_SSH_PORT=$(q "$VM_SSH_PORT")"
        echo "VM_SSH_USER=$(q "$VM_SSH_USER")"
        echo "VM_SSH_KEY=$(q "$(abs "$VM_SSH_KEY")")"
        echo "VM_KNOWN_HOSTS=$(q "$(abs "${VM_KNOWN_HOSTS:-known_hosts}")")"
    )
}

run_() {         # exit: 1 the host lacks a need (deps install), 65 the projects' needs clash,
                # 69 the VM doesn't meet them (or won't start), 75 busy with --no-wait; else COMMAND's
    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); D=$2
    shift 2
    KEEP=0; NOWAIT=""
    while :; do
        case ${1:-} in
            --keep-vm) KEEP=1; shift ;;
            --no-wait) NOWAIT=--no-wait; shift ;;
            --) shift; break ;;
            *) usage ;;
        esac
    done
    [ $# -gt 0 ] || usage
    [ -f "$D/.coworker/deps.json" ] || { echo "vms: no $D/.coworker/deps.json (README.md, \"Dependencies\")" >&2; exit 2; }
    P=$(basename "$(cd "$D" && pwd -P)")  # a project's name is its checkout directory's (the real one)
    "$DEPS" vm-claim "$VM" "$D" || exit $?
    lock "$VM" "$P" $NOWAIT -- run_locked "$@"
}

run_locked() {  # under the lock: start the VM if it's down, check it, COMMAND, stop it if started here
    eval "$(env_of "$VM")"
    export VM_HOME VM_OS VM_CONTAINER VM_SSH_HOST VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY VM_KNOWN_HOSTS
    STARTED=0
    if [ -n "$VM_CONTAINER" ] && [ "$(docker inspect -f '{{.State.Running}}' "$VM_CONTAINER" 2>/dev/null)" != true ]; then
        echo "starting $VM ($VM_CONTAINER)"
        docker start "$VM_CONTAINER" >/dev/null || { echo "vms: couldn't start $VM_CONTAINER" >&2; return 69; }
        STARTED=1
        trap 'stop_started; exit 130' INT TERM HUP
    fi
    rc=0
    "$DEPS" vm-guest "$VM" --wait "${COWORKER_VM_BOOT_WAIT:-900}" || rc=$?
    [ "$rc" = 0 ] && { "$@" || rc=$?; }
    stop_started
    return "$rc"
}

stop_started() {
    [ "$STARTED" = 1 ] || return 0
    STARTED=0
    if [ "$KEEP" = 1 ]; then
        echo "$VM left running (--keep-vm): stopping it is $P's"
    else
        echo "stopping $VM (this run started it)"
        docker stop -t 120 "$VM_CONTAINER" >/dev/null || echo "vms: couldn't stop $VM_CONTAINER" >&2
    fi
}

# -- building and updating a VM (README.md, "VM recipes") ------------------------------------------

vssh() {        # vssh no|yes COMMAND: ssh to the VM as vm.env says; "no": before known_hosts is written
    if [ "$1" = no ]; then kh=/dev/null; strict=no; else kh=$VM_KNOWN_HOSTS; strict=yes; fi
    "${COWORKER_SSH:-ssh}" -q -i "$VM_SSH_KEY" -p "$VM_SSH_PORT" -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 \
        -o "StrictHostKeyChecking=$strict" -o "UserKnownHostsFile=$kh" "$VM_SSH_USER@$VM_SSH_HOST" "$2"
}
wait_ssh() {    # wait_ssh no|yes SECONDS
    end=$(( $(date +%s) + $2 ))
    until vssh "$1" "echo up" 2>/dev/null | tr -d '\r' | grep -qx up; do
        [ "$(date +%s)" -lt "$end" ] || { echo "vms: $VM: no SSH after $2 s" >&2; return 69; }
        sleep "${COWORKER_VM_POLL:-15}"
    done
}
guest_build() {
    vssh yes '$v = Get-ItemProperty "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion"; "10.0.$($v.CurrentBuild).$($v.UBR)"' | tr -d '\r' | tail -1
}

create() {      # a human's call: it replaces the VM every claimant uses (exit 3 without --yes)
    [ $# -ge 1 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1"); shift
    YES=0
    [ "${1:-}" = --yes ] && YES=1
    [ "${COWORKER_UNATTENDED:-}" = 1 ] && YES=1
    R="$RECIPES/$VM"
    [ -f "$R/recipe.env" ] || { echo "vms: no recipe for $VM in $RECIPES (README.md, \"VM recipes\")" >&2; exit 1; }
    if [ "$YES" != 1 ]; then
        c=$(claims_of "$VM")
        echo "vms create $VM builds it from $R, replacing $DIR/$VM's (its disk is kept as storage-<date>-old)," >&2
        echo "for every project that claims it:${c:- none yet}. It takes an hour or more. A human's call:" >&2
        echo "    vms create $VM --yes" >&2
        exit 3
    fi
    mkdir -p "$DIR/$VM"
    lock "$VM" coworker -- create_locked
}

create_locked() {
    H="$DIR/$VM"
    . "$R/recipe.env"
    cd "$H" || return 1
    for f in ssh.sh scp.sh shot.sh keys.sh; do install -m 755 "$R/$f" "$f"; done
    install -m 644 "$R/update.ps1" update.ps1
    mkdir -p oem
    install -m 644 "$R/oem/install.bat" "$R/oem/vmctl.py" oem/
    [ -s password.txt ] || (umask 077; python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(18))' > password.txt)
    [ -s vm_key ] || ssh-keygen -q -t ed25519 -N '' -C "coworker $VM" -f vm_key
    cp vm_key.pub oem/authorized_key.pub
    if ! echo "$OPENSSH_SHA256  oem/OpenSSH-Win64.zip" | sha256sum -c --quiet >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        curl -fsSL -o oem/OpenSSH-Win64.zip.part "$OPENSSH_URL" || return 1
        echo "$OPENSSH_SHA256  oem/OpenSSH-Win64.zip.part" | sha256sum -c --quiet || { echo "vms: $OPENSSH_URL isn't the file the recipe pins" >&2; return 1; }
        mv oem/OpenSSH-Win64.zip.part oem/OpenSSH-Win64.zip
    fi
    C=coworker-$VM
    cat > vm.env <<END
# How projects reach this VM (the coworker README, "vm.env"), written by vms create from the recipe
VM_OS="$VM_OS"
VM_CONTAINER=$C
VM_SSH_HOST=127.0.0.1
VM_SSH_PORT=$SSH_PORT
VM_SSH_USER=$USERNAME
VM_SSH_KEY=vm_key
VM_KNOWN_HOSTS=known_hosts
END
    if docker inspect "$C" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        docker stop -t 120 "$C" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
        docker rm "$C" >/dev/null || return 1
    fi
    if [ -d storage ]; then
        old=storage-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M)-old
        mv storage "$old"
        echo "$VM: the old disk is $H/$old; delete it once the new VM works"
    fi
    mkdir storage
    cp oem/vmctl.py storage/vmctl.py
    set -- -v "$H/storage:/storage" -v "$H/oem:/oem"
    if [ -n "${ISO:-}" ] && [ -f "$HOMEDIR/downloads/$ISO" ]; then set -- "$@" -v "$HOMEDIR/downloads/$ISO:/boot.iso:ro"; fi
    docker run -d --name "$C" --device /dev/kvm --device /dev/net/tun --cap-add NET_ADMIN --stop-timeout 120 \
        -e VERSION="$WIN_VERSION" -e RAM_SIZE="$RAM" -e CPU_CORES="$CPUS" -e DISK_SIZE="$DISK" \
        -e USERNAME="$USERNAME" -e PASSWORD="$(cat password.txt)" -e USER_PORTS=22 \
        -p "127.0.0.1:$WEB_PORT:8006" -p "127.0.0.1:$RDP_PORT:3389" -p "127.0.0.1:$SSH_PORT:22" \
        "$@" "$IMAGE" >/dev/null || return 1
    rm -f known_hosts
    echo "$VM: installing $VM_OS (watch http://127.0.0.1:$WEB_PORT); SSH answers when setup has finished"
    eval "$(env_of "$VM")"
    wait_ssh no "${COWORKER_VM_INSTALL_WAIT:-7200}" || return $?
    host_keys || return $?
    update_rounds || return $?
    printf '%s  built from the recipe of coworker %s\n' "$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC')" "$(cat "$HOMEDIR/VERSION" 2>/dev/null || echo '?')" >> history
    echo "$VM: built; stopping it (vms run starts it when a project needs it)"
    docker stop -t 120 "$C" >/dev/null
}

host_keys() {   # known_hosts: the keys the guest says it has, as they answer on the port
    vssh no 'Get-Content C:\ProgramData\ssh\ssh_host_*_key.pub' | tr -d '\r' > .keys.guest
    "${COWORKER_SSH_KEYSCAN:-ssh-keyscan}" -p "$VM_SSH_PORT" "$VM_SSH_HOST" 2>/dev/null > .keys.scan
    : > known_hosts.new
    while read -r t k _; do
        grep " $t $k\$" .keys.scan >> known_hosts.new || true
    done < .keys.guest
    rm -f .keys.guest .keys.scan
    [ -s known_hosts.new ] || { rm -f known_hosts.new; echo "vms: $VM: no host key the guest names answers on port $VM_SSH_PORT" >&2; return 69; }
    mv known_hosts.new known_hosts
}

update_rounds() { # Windows Update as SYSTEM (update.ps1), rebooting as it asks, until nothing is left
    vssh yes 'New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force C:\coworker | Out-Null' >/dev/null || return 69
    i=0
    while [ "$i" -lt "${COWORKER_VM_UPDATE_ROUNDS:-8}" ]; do
        i=$((i + 1))
        "${COWORKER_SCP:-scp}" -q -i "$VM_SSH_KEY" -P "$VM_SSH_PORT" -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes -o "UserKnownHostsFile=$VM_KNOWN_HOSTS" \
            "$VM_HOME/update.ps1" "$VM_SSH_USER@$VM_SSH_HOST:C:/coworker/update.ps1" || return 69
        vssh yes "Remove-Item C:\coworker\update.result -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
            schtasks /create /tn coworker-update /tr 'powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\coworker\update.ps1' /sc once /st 23:59 /ru SYSTEM /rl HIGHEST /f | Out-Null
            schtasks /run /tn coworker-update | Out-Null" >/dev/null || return 69
        echo "$VM: Windows Update, round $i"
        end=$(( $(date +%s) + ${COWORKER_VM_UPDATE_WAIT:-10800} ))
        res=""
        while [ -z "$res" ]; do
            [ "$(date +%s)" -lt "$end" ] || { echo "vms: $VM: round $i didn't finish in ${COWORKER_VM_UPDATE_WAIT:-10800} s" >&2; return 1; }
            sleep "${COWORKER_VM_POLL:-15}"
            res=$(vssh yes 'Get-Content C:\coworker\update.result -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue' | tr -d '\r' | grep -E '^(DONE|FAILED)' || true)
        done
        echo "$VM: $res"
        case $res in FAILED*) echo "vms: $VM: Windows Update failed (C:\coworker\update.log)" >&2; return 1 ;; esac
        set -- $res
        inst=${2#installed=}; bad=${3#failed=}; boot=${4#reboot=}
        if [ "$boot" = 1 ]; then
            echo "$VM: restarting, as Windows Update asks"
            vssh yes 'shutdown /r /t 5' >/dev/null || true
            sleep "${COWORKER_VM_REBOOT_PAUSE:-90}"
            wait_ssh yes "${COWORKER_VM_BOOT_WAIT:-1800}" || return $?
            continue
        fi
        if [ "$inst" = 0 ]; then
            [ "$bad" = 0 ] || { echo "vms: $VM: $bad update(s) keep failing to install (C:\coworker\update.log)" >&2; return 1; }
            b=$(guest_build)
            printf '%s %s\n' "$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)" "$b" > "$VM_HOME/updated"
            echo "$VM: up to date, build $b"
            return 0
        fi
    done
    echo "vms: $VM: Windows Update still had updates after $i rounds" >&2
    return 1
}

update() {
    [ $# -ge 1 ] || usage
    VM=$(basename "$1")
    [ -f "$DIR/$VM/update.ps1" ] || { echo "vms: $DIR/$VM has no update.ps1: build it with vms create (README.md, \"VM recipes\")" >&2; exit 1; }
    lock "$VM" coworker -- update_locked
}

update_locked() {
    eval "$(env_of "$VM")"
    export VM_HOME VM_OS VM_CONTAINER VM_SSH_HOST VM_SSH_PORT VM_SSH_USER VM_SSH_KEY VM_KNOWN_HOSTS
    STARTED=0; KEEP=0; P=coworker
    if [ -n "$VM_CONTAINER" ] && [ "$(docker inspect -f '{{.State.Running}}' "$VM_CONTAINER" 2>/dev/null)" != true ]; then
        echo "starting $VM ($VM_CONTAINER)"
        docker start "$VM_CONTAINER" >/dev/null || { echo "vms: couldn't start $VM_CONTAINER" >&2; return 69; }
        STARTED=1
        trap 'stop_started; exit 130' INT TERM HUP
    fi
    rc=0
    wait_ssh yes "${COWORKER_VM_BOOT_WAIT:-900}" || rc=$?
    [ "$rc" = 0 ] && { update_rounds || rc=$?; }
    stop_started
    return "$rc"
}

list() {
    [ -d "$DIR" ] || { echo "no $DIR"; return 0; }
    cd "$DIR"
    names=$({ for f in *; do [ -d "$f" ] && echo "$f"; done
              for f in *.*; do [ -f "$f" ] || continue; s=${f##*.}
                  [ "$s" = lock ] || echo "${f%."$s"}"; done; } | sort -u)
    for v in $names; do
        c=$(claims_of "$v")
        if [ -f "$v/vm.env" ]; then what=$( (. "./$v/vm.env"; echo "${VM_OS:-a VM}") )
        else what="not set up yet (no $v/vm.env)"; fi
        use=free
        if [ -e "$v.lock" ] && ! ( flock -n 9 ) 9>>"$v.lock"; then use="in use: $(cat "$v.lock")"; fi
        if [ -n "$c" ]; then echo "$v | $what | claimed by$c | $use"; else echo "$v | $what | unclaimed | $use"; fi
    done
}

cmd=${1:-}
[ $# -gt 0 ] && shift
case $cmd in
    run) client; run_ "$@" ;;
    claim) client; claim "$@" ;;
    release) client; release "$@" ;;
    lock) client; lock "$@" ;;
    env) env_of "$@" ;;
    list) list ;;
    create) client; create "$@" ;;
    update) client; update "$@" ;;
    *) echo "$USAGE" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
